==============================================================================
SCOPE STATEMENT (do not let the numbers above imply more than this)
==============================================================================
  SHOWN     : the gate does not false-fire on 2 synthetic healthy curves, and
              fires on 2 synthetic broken ones with S at/just after the break;
              it does not false-fire on the one REAL healthy curve on disk.
  UNVERIFIED: that it catches a REAL collapse.  No collapsed run exists yet;
              CORAL (the one method with a documented late-epoch covariance
              blow-up, PROJECT.md 7.4) is the calibration case, pending the
              bake-off.  Do NOT promote this to a live early-stopper (Job 2)
              until that evidence exists.

  BAKE-OFF HOOK REQUIREMENT (one line, for the run spec):
    At every curve step, log one extra column per fold --
      agreement = Spearman(DA_checkpoint scores, BaselineA_final scores)
      on that fold's UNLABELED target pool (target_fold{k}) --
    so this gate can read live-produced curves without re-loading checkpoints.
